      "Per-person method: we use Statistics Finland's own 'consumption expenditure per consumption unit per month' series. A consumption unit uses the modified OECD scale (first adult = 1, other persons 14+ = 0.5, children = 0.3), so for a ONE-PERSON household the figure equals spending per person. This is the fairest comparison for a single bank account holder.",
      "Values are 2022 euros. Prices rose 6.2 % (2023), 1.6 % (2024) and 0.3 % (2025) since then; multiply by 'inflation.cumulative_factor_2022_to_2025' for a rough 2025-price view (an estimate, not an official statistic).",
